# serial_three_clients_board -- a region one client writes and the others
# read, with no channel joining any of them.
#
# `serial_three_clients_menu.bron` published one region every domain may
# reach and only the virtualiser may write. That shape is what let a reader
# of the grants say something true and narrow: a region two clients only
# read is a fact they agree about rather than a hazard between them.
#
# This declaration adds the case that shape cannot reach. `board` is written
# by `client_a` and read by `client_b` and `client_c`, and no channel joins
# any client to any other. So a reader of the grants alone must answer that
# `client_a` conflicts with both of the others at every instant -- they share
# a region one side may write, which is exactly the hazard the grant reading
# exists to catch.
#
# That answer is true of the domain and false of most of its work. A client
# is handed a line narrowed to the arcs it names this turn, so a `client_a`
# peeking its own `back_a` holds no capability to `board` at all while it
# runs. The ceiling says the two contend; the line handed over says they
# never touch. Both readings are honest about different things, and the
# document is written to hold them apart.
#
# Nothing else moves from the menu declaration: the same four domains, the
# same three channels to the virtualiser, the same private regions and arcs,
# and `menu` still published by the virtualiser to every client.
#
# Read whole by `caravan/read.rye`; exercised by `caravan/unhand.rye`.

system serial_three_clients_board

domain serial_virt
domain client_a
domain client_b
domain client_c

channel serial_virt client_a
channel serial_virt client_b
channel serial_virt client_c

region ask_a 4096
region back_a 4096
region taken_a 64
region ask_b 4096
region back_b 4096
region taken_b 64
region ask_c 4096
region back_c 4096
region taken_c 64
region menu 4096
region board 4096

grant ask_a client_a rw
grant ask_a serial_virt r
grant back_a serial_virt rw
grant back_a client_a r
grant taken_a client_a rw
grant ask_b client_b rw
grant ask_b serial_virt r
grant back_b serial_virt rw
grant back_b client_b r
grant taken_b client_b rw
grant ask_c client_c rw
grant ask_c serial_virt r
grant back_c serial_virt rw
grant back_c client_c r
grant taken_c client_c rw
grant menu serial_virt rw
grant menu client_a r
grant menu client_b r
grant menu client_c r
grant board client_a rw
grant board client_b r
grant board client_c r
